            {
              "system": "http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/condition-ver-status",
              "code": "provisional"
            }
          ]
        },
        "note": [
          {
            "text": "Right eye more commonly affected than alternating exotropia. Stable over the last approximately 6 weeks, with mild symptoms, preserved visual acuity, normal fundus and basic neurological examination. Comitant pattern without a vertical component or current red flags suggesting an acute neurological or intracranial process."
          }
        ]
